15
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:41,109
Let's start with what drives the need for firms to migrate from the existing observability tool set.

16
00:01:41,109 --> 00:01:47,670
Do you have a story or an example where a firm needed to migrate from their existing observability tool set?

17
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:51,670
Yeah, actually a lot.

18
00:01:51,670 --> 00:02:01,990
Basically every customer of ground cover not all of them but most of them are coming from some legacy vendors they most R&amp;Ds already use observability platform.

19
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:10,229
So when they want to move to the new observability platform more modern that rely on bring your own cloud

20
00:02:10,229 --> 00:02:24,550
and EVPF the main challenge is how do we migrate all the hard work we did as an R&amp;D organization right you can think about it as dashboards

21
00:02:24,550 --> 00:02:34,391
right most of R&amp;D has some kind of top 10 top 20 we often seen hundreds of dashboards across the entire R&amp;D. It could be monitors.

22
00:02:34,391 --> 00:02:48,949
So imagine that you rely on specific alerts to wake you up at night to make sure your software is actually behaving as as you expect it to be and that your customers get their SLAs's.

23
